      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being adrift, like a ghost in your own life, is exhausting, and it makes sense that the idea of \"going back\" feels impossible. If the person you used to be feels like they've vanished, perhaps the goal isn't to restore what was, but to simply find a way to make this current, hollow feeling a little less unbearable. Sometimes, the only way forward is to take the smallest step toward an acceptance of the present, even if it's just a small, quiet act of self-kindness.",
      "source": "target",
